CEFR-FR demo corpus — attribution and license
==============================================

The file demo_corpora/cefr_fr_corpus.csv combines two French CEFR-labeled
text collections from the UniversalCEFR project on HuggingFace, fetched and
merged by R/artefact_builders/fetch_universalcefr_fr.R:

  - readme_fr — 1,669 sentence-level texts labeled A1-C2, drawn from the
    ReadMe++ benchmark.
      Naous, T., Ryan, M. J., Lukin, S., & Xu, W. (2024). ReadMe++:
      Benchmarking Multilingual Language Models for Multi-Domain
      Readability Assessment. Proceedings of EMNLP 2024.
      https://huggingface.co/datasets/UniversalCEFR/readme_fr

  - kwiqiz_fr — 344 document-level texts (full articles) labeled with CEFR
    levels A1-C1, sourced from the Kwiziq language-learning platform.
      https://huggingface.co/datasets/UniversalCEFR/kwiqiz_fr

Both are public, non-gated HuggingFace dataset repos (no login required).

Source dataset collection
--------------------------
  UniversalCEFR (https://huggingface.co/UniversalCEFR) re-indexes existing
  CEFR-labeled corpora into a common schema (title, lang, source_name,
  format, category, cefr_level, license, text).

